            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A decent residential lawn tractor with a hydrostatic transmission and a reputable engine typically costs around $2,300 to $3,800. That range buys meaningfully better durability than entry machines. Below about $2,000 you usually give up transmission and deck quality; above about $4,000 you are into premium tractors, garden tractors and better-built zero-turns."
